      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For the fishing game I've had to start going to my home world before quitting for the evening, just to make sure my FISH progress is saved.\n\nI think asking to exit the game from the settings menu should effectively be a \"save and quit\", be willing to give a game world a minute or two to save.\n\nI'd like all the quitting method to save first, but I can understand why VRChat can't hang around if given an external exit signal",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-06T14:44:13.387Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Exit the game normally from the Settings menu, and it will not trigger OnPlayerLeave() locally.  This means persistence checks can't fire for the player. (eg; A player can't auto-save a game world when exiting).",
